  maybe toward the $2,500–3,000 end — because the car has rental/loaner
  history, and the factory 161-point inspection plus a 6-year unlimited-mile
  warranty is exactly the hedge you want against how a non-personal-use car was
  treated. Cheapest price and the strongest insurance against its own main risk.
  - General rule for the rest of your shopping: treat CPO as a ~$2k tiebreaker,
  never a $5k+ justification. If a dealer wants materially more than that for
  the badge, you're better off buying the cleaner non-CPO car — on this
  platform, reliability is doing most of the warranty's job for free.

